  "answer": "The implementation is complete. Let me verify it handles all the specified cases correctly by tracing through the logic:\n\n**Requirements check:**\n\n1. **`input` must be a string; otherwise throw `TypeError`** ✓ — `if (typeof input !== 'string') throw new TypeError(...)`\n\n2. **Split only on literal commas** ✓ — `input.split(',')` splits on the literal `,` character only (not regex).\n\n3. **Trim surrounding JavaScript whitespace** ✓ — `.trim()` removes leading/trailing JS whitespace (spaces, tabs, newlines, etc.).\n\n4. **Collapse each nonempty internal whitespace run to one ASCII space** ✓ — `.replace(/\\s+/g, ' ')` collapses runs of whitespace to a single ASCII space. Since `.trim()` already removed surrounding whitespace, only internal runs remain.\n\n5. **Lowercase with `String.prototype.toLowerCase()`** ✓ — `.toLowerCase()`.\n\n6. **Discard empty normalized parts** ✓ — `if (normalized === '') continue;`.\n\n7. **Return unique normalized tags in first-occurrence order** ✓ — `Set` tracks seen values; `result` preserves insertion order.\n\n8. **Comparisons case-sensitive after normalization** ✓ — Since normalization lowercases, differently-cased spellings collapse to the same string and are deduplicated (e.g., `Alpha` and `alpha` → both `alpha`).\n\n9. **Empty or delimiter-only string returns `[]`** ✓ — e.g., `''` → `['']` → skipped; `',,,'` → all empty → `[]`.\n\n**Public tests trace:**\n- `parseTags('red,blue,green')` → `['red', 'blue', 'green']` ✓\n- `parseTags('  Red , , BLUE  ,')` → parts: `'  Red '`→`'red'`, `' '`→`''`(skip), `' BLUE  '`→`'blue'`, `''`→`''`(skip) → `['red', 'blue']` ✓\n- `parseTags('Alpha,beta,alpha,BETA,gamma')` → `'alpha'`, `'beta'`, `'alpha'`(dup skip), `'beta'`(dup skip), `'gamma'` → `['alpha', 'beta', 'gamma']` ✓\n\nThe named export `parseTags` is preserved, and the public tests were not modified.",
